WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:32.660
<b>Several Hours Ago...</b>

3
00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:39.360
Dang it!

4
00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:43.710
Thing is, I got beef
with the World Government.

5
00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:46.010
Apparently, they're
not just killing Stella,

6
00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:47.970
they're gonna kill me, too!

7
00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:53.680
<b>Emperor Red Hair's Pirate Crew</b>

8
00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:51.690
So rude, am I right?
Am I right?!

9
00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:53.690
Hey! Say it's rude!

10
00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:55.350
Correct. It's very rude.

11
00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:56.520
You paused!

12
00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:59.760
But anyways, I got a plan
to turn this thing around!

13
00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:04.520
So your job is to help
mama kill some people

14
00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:06.680
who are annoying her, okay?

15
00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:09.650
I shut the Frontier Dome,
so I want everyone in here dead,

16
00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:12.350
except me, Stella,
and the hostages underground.

17
00:02:12.430 --> 00:02:14.110
Say "roger" if you got all that.

18
00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:16.190
Roger!

19
00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:18.930
Sweetness. Now, when you
start kicking their butts,

20
00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:20.750
problem is, the Punks'll go,

21
00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:22.910
"Wait, who's ordering
these things?"

22
00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:24.550
And then they'll catch me!

23
00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:26.530
I can't beat 'em in a fair fight,

24
00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:28.550
so I need a backup plan!

25
00:02:28.630 --> 00:02:30.320
Cue S-Snake!

26
00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:31.300
Yes?

27
00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:32.920
You gotta petrify me.

28
00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:34.750
And do it in front
of them, all right?

29
00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:35.680
Right.

30
00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:38.120
Then come back and undo
it when no one's looking!

31
00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:39.510
Roger.

32
00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:42.060
Oh! Before I forget,

33
00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:45.730
there's a couple places
in the lab you shouldn't blow up.

34
00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:51.080
This is important,
so listen real carefully.

35
00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:55.090
Ready. Steady. Hunt!

36
00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:19.170
Everyone
on the ship! Quick!

37
00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:22.030
We need
to get off Egghead, now!

38
00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:43.790
<b>The Land of War, Elbaph
New World</b>

39
00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:51.640
Everyone ready?
Let's get to work.

40
00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:52.430
Yeah!

41
00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:55.360
Kid Pirate!

42
00:03:57.910 --> 00:04:00.090
Only a fool would
oppose our chief.

43
00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:01.930
You're gonna die today.

44
00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:05.820
I told you!

45
00:04:05.690 --> 00:04:07.940
No!
Not the frog thing!

46
00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:10.740
Get lost or croak, ribbit!

47
00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:11.400
<b>Captain "Frog-Toes" Gerotini
Puddle Pirates</b>

48
00:04:12.990 --> 00:04:15.640
Yeah! What he said!

49
00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:18.080
Pops,
your dentures!

50
00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:18.740
<b>Bandmaster Fuga "the Addenturer"
Social Club</b>

51
00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:21.250
Away with you,
fools! I do not like you!

52
00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:24.760
You will never reach Chiefie!

53
00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:29.050
Go away! Now! Or I
shall be cross with you!

54
00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:32.840
<b>Pururu "the Brr-rave"
Bourgeois Pirates</b>

55
00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:34.830
Is Red Hair mocking us?

56
00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:37.050
These can't be his real allies.

57
00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:41.640
How do these clowns even
survive in the New World?

58
00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:43.250
I get
what you mean,

59
00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:45.740
but he's got a few
famous names in there.

60
00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:47.480
Don't get sloppy.

61
00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:51.370
Whether they're weak or strong,
I'm not here to show mercy.

62
00:04:57.840 --> 00:04:59.510
Are we
ready to set sail?

63
00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:00.740
Hey, Boss!

64
00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:02.930
The other crews
went out to stop Kid!

65
00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:04.760
Then tell
them to retreat!

66
00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:06.490
I don't want them
dying for nothing.

67
00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:09.840
Whoa, whoa,
whoa! Wait, wait, wait!

68
00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:15.740
C'mon, Chief!
What are you tryin' to pull?

69
00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:17.960
I think I
should be asking you that.

70
00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:19.140
We'll handle this!

71
00:05:19.220 --> 00:05:21.020
They won't lay
a damn finger on you!

72
00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:22.110
That's right!

73
00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:26.220
Thanks, guys.
For the offer, I mean.

74
00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:28.470
But seriously, stay put.

75
00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:38.990
Please don't go!

76
00:05:39.030 --> 00:05:41.750
At least let us
fight beside you!

77
00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:44.770
Huh?

78
00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:48.430
Whoa, that's enough! Easy!

79
00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:51.640
Aw, c'mon! You can't
be takin' off already!

80
00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:49.700
Aw, come on!

81
00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:53.220
Yeah, you just got here!

82
00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:55.200
We've hardly had
a chance to chat!

83
00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:56.760
We
got places to be.

84
00:05:56.770 --> 00:05:59.110
I was just stoppin'
here for a quick drink.

85
00:05:59.110 --> 00:06:02.820
I'm sorry, but let me
go, guys. C'mon.

86
00:06:01.470 --> 00:06:02.270
Come on.

87
00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:07.310
A big shot showed up because
I bummed around too long.

88
00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:11.400
Alright, one more
time. Tell the ships to retreat!

89
00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:12.600
You know I'd take you,

90
00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:15.260
but I can't be seen
with a bunch of weaklings.

91
00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:19.850
Tell us
how you really feel!

92
00:06:19.930 --> 00:06:21.710
What does it
matter if we're weak?

93
00:06:21.790 --> 00:06:24.450
We're invincible as long
as we have your flag!

94
00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:26.120
Don't get
too comfortable, Oli.

95
00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:28.350
My flag can't scare
off old age for ya.

96
00:06:28.550 --> 00:06:30.910
Ha-ha! Do you hear
the way he talks to me?

97
00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:32.860
No respect for his elders!

98
00:06:32.860 --> 00:06:35.310
Hurry up, Boss!
Your fans can wait.

99
00:06:35.570 --> 00:06:36.370
Oh, please.

100
00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:39.120
Eh, we'll wrap this up in two
shakes of a drumstick.

101
00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:39.830
Don't worry.

102
00:06:39.990 --> 00:06:43.160
Don't get cocky. Kid's
worth three billion, y'know?

103
00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:46.490
They grow up fast these days.
You gotta be careful.

104
00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:51.090
But they had
a hell of a fight in Wano.

105
00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:52.960
Does it look like
their wounds have healed?

106
00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:56.240
Uh-huh. They're
in tip-top shape.

107
00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:57.990
Definitely ready for a fight.

108
00:06:58.400 --> 00:06:59.630
That's good to hear.

109
00:06:59.990 --> 00:07:03.000
What about Blackbeard?
Any updates yet?

110
00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:06.840
No. All we know is that
he left Pirate Island.

111
00:07:07.310 --> 00:07:10.070
I was so sure he'd show
up in the Land of Wano.

112
00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:11.970
Hongo!

113
00:07:13.480 --> 00:07:15.680
Ready. Here's
your intel on Kid.

114
00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:16.720
We're so proud of you,

115
00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:18.340
turning your homework
in on time.

116
00:07:18.490 --> 00:07:21.460
That's enough! We
got a ship to load!

117
00:07:21.510 --> 00:07:24.630
I see. So he's
from the South Blue.

118
00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:27.780
And it looks like he's gone
on quite the rampage.

119
00:07:31.370 --> 00:07:33.010
How many
ships are there?

120
00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:34.180
Nine total.

121
00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:38.270
There are some faces I've
seen on wanted posters.

122
00:07:54.470 --> 00:07:55.820
I don't care!

123
00:07:55.900 --> 00:07:57.540
I don't care
who we're up against!

124
00:07:57.620 --> 00:08:03.200
Let them come!

125
00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:06.130
I'll wipe them all out
in ten seconds flat!

126
00:08:06.940 --> 00:08:08.750
Here it comes!

127
00:08:08.830 --> 00:08:09.790
The ship!

128
00:08:14.410 --> 00:08:17.840
He's pulling
the ship! Do something!

129
00:08:18.050 --> 00:08:18.830
What is that?

130
00:08:18.910 --> 00:08:20.170
A Cannon.

131
00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:23.210
I'll crush you under my feet!

132
00:08:23.450 --> 00:08:25.710
I'm going straight to the top,

133
00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:29.550
and I won't let anyone
get in my way!

134
00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:41.520
See you in hell!

135
00:09:11.350 --> 00:09:17.940
C'mon, Red Hair!
The next one's for you!

136
00:09:17.940 --> 00:09:21.940
Damn it. Tell the fleet
to spread out!

137
00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:23.450
You see somethin', Boss?

138
00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:25.870
Dorry! Brogy! Get ready!

139
00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:27.670
We were born ready!

140
00:09:29.780 --> 00:09:30.900
Hard to port!

141
00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:39.920
Too much power.
He'll kill them!

142
00:09:47.460 --> 00:09:49.890
I guess he saw
a future he didn't like.

143
00:09:57.760 --> 00:09:59.440
See you in hell!

144
00:10:01.230 --> 00:10:03.650
Should've
expected this!

145
00:10:17.060 --> 00:10:20.870
You kept me waiting!

146
00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:26.560
Divine Departure.

147
00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:32.430
Open your eyes,
please! Get up!

148
00:11:32.430 --> 00:11:36.390
Damn it! Killer got
hurt trying to protect him!

149
00:11:44.370 --> 00:11:46.040
No! Stop, Red Hair!

150
00:11:46.040 --> 00:11:48.160
We surrender!
Please, have mercy!

151
00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:51.670
We're begging you,
please don't kill our boss!

152
00:11:54.670 --> 00:11:56.630
Go, Emma. Bring them out.

153
00:11:56.700 --> 00:11:58.830
– Huh?
– Hurry!

154
00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:04.350
These are
our Road Poneglyphs!

155
00:12:04.430 --> 00:12:06.060
All the ones we've got!

156
00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:10.090
You can have them,
just please let us live!

157
00:12:21.210 --> 00:12:24.170
C'mon, Chief! Time to go!

158
00:12:39.510 --> 00:12:43.090
Hey, you guys.
Look over there!

159
00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:53.520
It's not over.
Something's coming!

160
00:13:05.660 --> 00:13:08.320
Hey, little ones, you
know what happens

161
00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:10.910
when you point a gun
at someone's home, right?

162
00:13:13.660 --> 00:13:17.100
You better be ready for them
to start shooting back.

163
00:13:21.930 --> 00:13:24.630
Hakoku!

164
00:14:00.550 --> 00:14:03.440
Thus,
the battle at Elbaph ended.

165
00:14:04.130 --> 00:14:05.680
Eustass
"Captain" Kid,

166
00:14:05.680 --> 00:14:07.970
with a bounty of three
billion berries,

167
00:14:07.970 --> 00:14:12.020
fell alongside his crew,
the Kid Pirates.

168
00:14:12.520 --> 00:14:14.400
It was a massacre.
